message: "If you use this tool or its rubric, please cite it as below."
title: "fair-repo-audit"
abstract: >-
  A static, client-side web tool that scores the FAIR metadata quality of any
  DataCite or OAI-PMH repository against 14 FAIR sub-principles, with
  concept-completeness profiles, per-record heatmaps, temporal trends and a
  side-by-side compare mode. It also scores a repository's own API against what
  it publishes, scores each registration cohort separately, replays the audit
  log of a single DOI, and reads a monthly scoring history produced by a
  scheduled job the user runs in their own repository. Every mode runs entirely in
  the visitor's browser and uploads nothing. Multilingual (EN/ES/DE).
  The open twin of the hosted Repo MetAudits service: the scoring engine is a
  faithful, fully-readable port, so scores match across both tools.
